<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  The General Electric J79-GE-15, the F-4C's engine, for JSBSim v1.3.3's turbine. FSG's own file: new in
  FSG, milestone 3 (docs/milestones/3.md, pull request 3). JSBSim finds it in the aircraft's own Engines
  folder before it looks in its shared engine folder.

  The two ratings are the flight manual's. T.O. 1F-4C-1 (1 October 1970), section I: "the J79-15 engine is
  rated at 10,900 pounds thrust at Mil power, while Max power is rated at 17,000". Verified (read);
  tests/f4c.test.js reads both back from a run at sea level, standing still.

  The afterburner is JSBSim's method 2: the throttle the engine is given runs 0 to 1 from idle to MIL and
  1 to 2 through the afterburner. The aircraft file's throttle system gives it that (aircraft/f4c/f4c.xml).

  How thrust changes with speed and height (pull request 11). Nobody publishes it for the J79-GE-15, so the
  MIL and afterburner tables below are JSBSim's own generic J79 (jsbsim-data/engine/J79-GE-11A.xml, made by
  Aeromatic 0.8, JSBSim v1.3.3), anchored to NASA CR-2144's F-4C (its trimmed lift and drag plot, figure IV-9):
    - full afterburner equals CR-2144's drag along its zero-excess-thrust line, at Mach 1.0, 1.2, 1.4, 1.6,
      1.8 and 2.0 (47,800 to 56,800 ft): Verified against the record, flown in tests/f4c-numbers.test.js;
    - full afterburner equals CR-2144's drag at sea level where its speed restriction ends the envelope,
      Mach 1.14 (the flight manual's 750 knots is Mach 1.134 there): the same;
    - between and beyond those anchors the shape is JSBSim's, scaled by a factor for each Mach row that runs
      straight with height (Reasoned); beyond Mach 2.0, where CR-2144's line ends, Mach 2.0's row is
      held; its empty 60,000 ft column is its own lapse carried on.
  tools/f4c-thrust.mjs makes the two tables, with every anchor's arithmetic, and says exactly how. The tables
  are written there and nowhere by hand; the test holds this file to the tool cell for cell. Sea-level static
  thrust is unchanged (10,900 and 17,000 lb; tests/f4c.test.js).

  Still JSBSim's generic J79 as it is, Reasoned and not tuned: the idle table; idle at 53% (the flight
  manual's idle speed is not yet read into this file), no bypass, and Aeromatic's fuel consumption figures,
  which change nothing while the game freezes the fuel.
-->
<turbine_engine name="J79-GE-15">
  <milthrust>   10900.0 </milthrust>
  <maxthrust>   17000.0 </maxthrust>
  <bypassratio>     0.0 </bypassratio>
  <tsfc>            0.95 </tsfc>
  <atsfc>           1.90 </atsfc>
  <idlen1>          0.0 </idlen1>
  <idlen2>         53.0 </idlen2>
  <maxn1>         100.0 </maxn1>
  <maxn2>         100.0 </maxn2>
  <augmented>         1 </augmented>
  <augmethod>         2 </augmethod>
  <injected>          0 </injected>

  <function name="IdleThrust">
   <table>
    <independentVar lookup="row">velocities/mach</independentVar>
    <independentVar lookup="column">atmosphere/density-altitude</independentVar>
    <tableData>
         -10000     0     10000   20000   30000   40000   50000   60000
     0.0  0.0430  0.0488  0.0528  0.0694  0.0899  0.1183  0.1467  0.0
